      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It's not wrong to want the pain to end—that's just your mind trying to find a way out of a room with no doors. Going to where he is would end the loneliness, yes, but it would also end every possibility of ever feeling the sun again, of ever finding a new voice in that quiet. You're not waiting to be with him; you're waiting for permission to stop hurting, and that permission doesn't have to come from death. The silence isn't lonely because he's gone—it's lonely because you're still here, and that means you still have a chance to make it yours.",
